   "title": {
    "en": "Standard electrode potentials"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "The standard hydrogen electrode is given a potential of 0.00 V, and other couples are measured against it under standard conditions. A more negative E° means a stronger reducing agent (Li is the strongest); a more positive E° means a stronger oxidising agent (F₂ is the strongest). The cell potential is $E°_{cell} = E°_{cathode} − E°_{anode}$.",
    "kn": "ಪ್ರಮಾಣಿತ ಹೈಡ್ರೋಜನ್ ವಿದ್ಯುದ್ವಾರದ ವಿಭವ 0.00 V. ಹೆಚ್ಚು ಋಣಾತ್ಮಕ E° ಎಂದರೆ ಬಲವಾದ ಅಪಕರ್ಷಕ; ಹೆಚ್ಚು ಧನಾತ್ಮಕ E° ಎಂದರೆ ಬಲವಾದ ಉತ್ಕರ್ಷಕ."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "E°(Zn²⁺/Zn) = −0.76 V"
    },
    {
     "en": "E°(Cu²⁺/Cu) = +0.34 V"
    },
    {
     "en": "E°(Ag⁺/Ag) = +0.80 V"
    },
    {
     "en": "A metal reduces the ions of any metal with higher E°"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "The standard hydrogen electrode is given a potential of 0.00 V, and other couples are measured against it under standard conditions. A more negative E° means a stronger reducing agent (Li is the strongest); a more positive E° means a stronger oxidising agent (F₂ is the strongest). The cell potential is E°cell = E°cathode − E°anode.",
    "kn": "ಪ್ರಮಾಣಿತ ಹೈಡ್ರೋಜನ್ ವಿದ್ಯುದ್ವಾರದ ವಿಭವ 0.00 V. ಹೆಚ್ಚು ಋಣಾತ್ಮಕ E° ಎಂದರೆ ಬಲವಾದ ಅಪಕರ್ಷಕ; ಹೆಚ್ಚು ಧನಾತ್ಮಕ E° ಎಂದರೆ ಬಲವಾದ ಉತ್ಕರ್ಷಕ."
